#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162081 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161894 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac9e7d-ea92-5cd3-af26-4c902196e80b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Line Integrals of Unity"}] :question/id #uuid "55e8e57f-7f9e-529a-aa1b-24e1d86c4133" :question/math-academy-id "e-9470" :question/problem "![](images/76/765415456d7f33c3558e08e7c4fc01ef3e80961c1e073a210033d91741d78f60.png)\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s,$ where $C$ is the arc of a semicircle of radius $4$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $C$ is a semicircle of radius $r = 4.$ Its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L=\\pi r=4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = 4\\pi.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac9e7d-ea92-5cd3-af26-4c902196e80b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050089} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050289} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050975}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543805 :question-generator/id #uuid "266305d9-55b0-5056-b70a-a675c8503e54" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186162081.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac9e7d-ea92-5cd3-af26-4c902196e80b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Line Integrals of Unity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9753b03f-5368-57b2-af6c-e7dbe0c7a32b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159177} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3bba85-4f43-5945-9af3-289916125d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159178} {:answ